      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start, but i noticed the score for that explanation was actually pretty low in the system—only around 1,300 characters. i know i said not to use filler, but for the student portal to actually surface this as a \"primary resource,\" it really needs to be much more substantial. \n\ncould you expand this significantly? try to go deeper into the derivation or perhaps the physical implications (like why this matters for the stability of atoms or the concept of zero-point energy). i'm looking for a much more massive, exhaustive deep-dive here so it hits a higher score in the library, but again, just make sure the extra content is actually substantive and not just repetitive fluff.",
